+## Byte-only Blueprint admission, 2026-10-25
+
+Blueprint's adopted native decoder supersedes the inherited structural admission policy above. Shared classification parsing uses the already admitted byte allowance and retains exact-number and duplicate-key checks. It no longer inherits global depth, value-count or numeric-token limits. LLM Wire introduces no replacement structural policy: valid deep, wide and large-number JSON reaches a custom wire decoder when it fits its byte allowance. TypeSafe's domain probability/range/underflow checks remain unchanged. Malformed JSON still fails before a custom decoder is invoked, including during receipt restoration.
